691:    <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="index.html" class="nav-link">Output Streaming Configuration</a></li>
693:    <li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page"><span class="ellipsis">Output Rail Streaming</span></li>
710:  <section class="tex2jax_ignore mathjax_ignore" id="output-rail-streaming">
711:<h1>Output Rail Streaming<a class="headerlink" href="#output-rail-streaming" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h1>
712:<p>Configure how output rails process streamed tokens under <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">rails.output.streaming</span></code>.</p>
719:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
721:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">chunk_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">200</span>
722:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">context_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50</span>
723:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">stream_first</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">True</span>
741:<td><p>Must be <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">True</span></code> to use <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_async()</span></code> with output rails</p></td>
743:<tr class="row-odd"><td><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">chunk_size</span></code></p></td>
746:<td><p>Number of tokens per chunk that output rails process</p></td>
748:<tr class="row-even"><td><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">context_size</span></code></p></td>
753:<tr class="row-odd"><td><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_first</span></code></p></td>
756:<td><p>If <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">True</span></code>, the client receives tokens before output rails run on the chunk</p></td>
766:<p>When you configure output rails and want to use <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_async()</span></code>, set this to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">True</span></code>.</p>
768:<div class="highlight-text notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>stream_async() cannot be used when output rails are configured but
769:rails.output.streaming.enabled is False. Either set
770:rails.output.streaming.enabled to True in your configuration, or use
776:<h4>chunk_size<a class="headerlink" href="#chunk-size" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h4>
777:<p>The number of tokens buffered before output rails run.</p>
785:<h4>context_size<a class="headerlink" href="#context-size" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h4>
787:<p>This helps output rails make consistent decisions across chunk boundaries. For example, if a sentence spans two chunks, the context ensures the rail can evaluate the complete sentence.</p>
791:<h4>stream_first<a class="headerlink" href="#stream-first" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h4>
792:<p>Controls when tokens are streamed relative to output rail processing:</p>
794:<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">True</span></code> (default): The client receives each chunk of tokens before output rails process that chunk. This provides faster time-to-first-token, but if a rail blocks the content, the user has already received the tokens. The stream terminates with a JSON error on violation.</p></li>
795:<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">False</span></code>: Output rails process each chunk before the client receives tokens. The user never sees blocked content, but time-to-first-token increases by the rail execution time per chunk.</p></li>
803:<p>Output rail streaming requires using the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_async()</span></code> method:</p>
808:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
814:<p>The top-level <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">streaming:</span> <span class="pre">True</span></code> field is deprecated and no longer required. Use <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_async()</span></code> directly instead.</p>
820:<section id="basic-output-rail-streaming">
821:<h3>Basic Output Rail Streaming<a class="headerlink" href="#basic-output-rail-streaming" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
826:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
828:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">chunk_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">200</span>
829:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">context_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50</span>
833:<section id="parallel-output-rails-with-streaming">
834:<h3>Parallel Output Rails With Streaming<a class="headerlink" href="#parallel-output-rails-with-streaming" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
835:<p>For parallel execution of multiple output rails during streaming:</p>
843:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
845:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">chunk_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">200</span>
846:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">context_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50</span>
847:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">stream_first</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">True</span>
858:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
860:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">chunk_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">50</span>
861:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">context_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">20</span>
862:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">stream_first</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">True</span>
867:<p>With <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_first:</span> <span class="pre">True</span></code>, the client receives tokens before output rails run. If a rail blocks the content, the user has already received the tokens up to that point. The stream terminates with a JSON error object when it detects a violation.</p>
872:<p>For maximum safety with rails applied before streaming:</p>
877:<span class="w">    </span><span class="nt">streaming</span><span class="p">:</span>
879:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">chunk_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">300</span>
880:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">context_size</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">75</span>
881:<span class="w">      </span><span class="nt">stream_first</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="l l-Scalar l-Scalar-Plain">False</span>
890:<li><p><strong>Token Buffering</strong>: The system buffers tokens from the LLM until <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">chunk_size</span></code> tokens accumulate.</p></li>
891:<li><p><strong>Streaming or Rail Execution</strong> (depends on <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_first</span></code>):</p>
893:<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_first:</span> <span class="pre">True</span></code> (default): The client receives the new tokens immediately, then output rails run on the chunk (including context). If the rails block the content, the stream terminates with a JSON error, while the client receives the tokens up to that point.</p></li>
894:<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">stream_first:</span> <span class="pre">False</span></code>: Output rails run on the chunk first. The client receives the new tokens only if rails pass. If the rails block the content, the client never receives the tokens.</p></li>
897:<li><p><strong>Context Overlap</strong>: The system retains the last <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">context_size</span></code> tokens from the current chunk and prepends them to the next chunk’s processing context. This gives rails visibility across chunk boundaries.</p></li>
901:<h3>stream_first: True (default)<a class="headerlink" href="#stream-first-true-default" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
902:<div class="highlight-text notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>Buffer fills to chunk_size
906:  Run output rails on [context + new tokens]
914:<h3>stream_first: False<a class="headerlink" href="#stream-first-false" title="Link to this heading">#</a></h3>
915:<div class="highlight-text notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>Buffer fills to chunk_size
917:  Run output rails on [context + new tokens]
926:<p>The client receives only new tokens. Output rails use the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">context_size</span></code> tokens solely for processing context:</p>
931:                        └── context_size ──┘  └── new tokens ───────┘
947:<span class="c1"># stream_async() automatically uses output rail streaming when configured</span>
